# What `COPY . .` must not take.
#
# Without this file the build context was 151 MB, and the image carried:
#
#   .env            SECRET_KEY and WDASH_ENCRYPTION_KEY
#   data/wdash.db   local accounts and their password hashes, the audit
#                   trail, and the source credentials that .env's key
#                   decrypts — so the key and the ciphertext together
#   venv/           96 MB of the build host's interpreter, wrong platform
#   node_modules/   19 MB of build-time tooling
#   lab/.venv/      28 MB more of the same
#
# A published image is public. This is the same leak as committing the files,
# through a door nobody looks at.

# Secrets and state
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
data/*
!data/.gitkeep

# Environments and build tooling
venv/
.venv/
**/.venv/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Local runtime files that are not part of the product. The agent's spool is
# the monitor results it has not delivered yet — check outcomes and their
# error text, host names included — and it sits in the root of a checkout
# that ran `python -m wdash.agent` from there.
agent-spool*.jsonl

# Git worktrees made by tooling inside the checkout. Every pattern above is
# anchored at the context root, so a worktree under .claude/ is a second
# checkout that none of them reach: its own data/, its own .env, and its own
# venv, all copied in by `COPY . .`.
.claude/

# Not needed at runtime
.git/
.gitignore
tests/
lab/
kubernetes/
docs/
.kiro/
.vscode/
*.md
!README.md
package.json
package-lock.json

# Editor
.DS_Store
*.swp
